-- title:
--   Second coordinate detects vanishing of reductions on the ordinary corner
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$ and $p^{2} \nmid M$; $H$ is a subgroup of $(\mathbf Z/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for the divisibility $(M/p) \mid M$ is $1$ (hypothesis `hHp`); $S$ is a set of natural numbers; and `hin : ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H` asserts both that `HeckeInputsHAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M H ℓ` holds for every prime $\ell$ and that every $d \in (\mathbf Z/M)^{\times}$ is realised by an $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-automorphism $\sigma$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` with `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d σ`. Here `JH M H` is the group `Pic0 (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (xHFunctionFieldBar M H)` of degree-zero divisor classes modulo principal divisors, and [`TateModule p (JH M H)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) is the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in `JH M H` with $p^{n}x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$.
--
--   *Hecke data and the ordinary corner.* A commutative ring $\mathbb T$ is given, an algebra over $\mathbf Z_p$ acting on [`TateModule p (JH M H)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) compatibly with the $\mathbf Z_p$-action, faithfully in the sense of `hfaith` (an element annihilating every vector is zero). A map `op` sends each generator symbol in [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) — the symbols $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \notin S$ not dividing $M$, $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, and $\langle d\rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbf Z/M)^{\times}$ — to an element of $\mathbb T$ whose action on the Tate module is the operator [`ModularCurve.tateGenOpH M H S p`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L99) of that generator (`hop`), and the $\mathbf Z_p$-subalgebra generated by the range of `op` is all of $\mathbb T$ (`hgen`). Further, `S' : IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting 𝕋` supplies an integer $n$, idempotents $e_i$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ ($i \in$ `Fin n`) forming a complete orthogonal family of idempotents such that every maximal ideal of $\mathbb T$ occurs among the $\mathfrak m_i$ and $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j$ exactly when $i \neq j$; an index $i_0$ is fixed with `op (CohCarrier.Gen.U p _ hpM) ∉ S'.𝔪 i₀` (`hord`), the ordinarity of the corner at $i_0$.
--
--   *Arithmetic place and integral models.* `Pl` is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with `Pl.LiesOverPrime p` (that is, $p$ is a non-unit of `Pl`), with residue field of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed; `hj` records that `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion function field of the full modular group; `𝔛 : ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` is the integral model package at $p$ for level $\Gamma_M(M,H)$, with its curve model `𝔛.Meta` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ for `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, comparison isomorphism `𝔛.eeta`, cusp section `𝔛.εinf`, degeneracy maps `𝔛.π`, `𝔛.πw`, Atkin–Lehner isomorphism `𝔛.w`, diamond isomorphisms `𝔛.dia0`, smooth locus `𝔛.smoothLocus`, and special-fibre curve model `𝔛.Mfib` with structure maps `𝔛.efib`, `𝔛.comp`. `Λ : ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM Pl` consists of a section `Λ.σA` of the base over `Spec Pl` lifting `genPt p`, a scheme `Λ.X` with structure morphism `Λ.f`, a relative group law `Λ.L`, a bijection `Λ.pts` from `JH (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` to the sections of `Λ.f` over `genPt p`, and a bijection `Λ.ptsSp` from the Picard group `Pic0` of the residue-field function field `Fbar p M H hpM (ResidueField Pl)` to the sections of `Λ.f` over `resPt Pl` followed by `Λ.σA`. The hypothesis `hrepΛ` asserts that the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$-functor of the level-$\Gamma_N$ curve, cut out by the condition `algEquivZeroCut` (fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero of rigidified line bundles), is represented by the designation built from `Λ.X`, `Λ.f` and the unit section of `Λ.L`. Finally `O : ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM Pl hPl Λ` is the Néron object at $p$ for `JH M H`, with scheme `O.G`, structure morphism `O.g`, commutative relative group law `O.L`, point dictionary `O.pts : JH M H ≃` sections of `O.g` over `genPt p`, Hecke endomorphisms `O.hecke`, toric rank `O.toricRank`, supersingular pairing finset `O.ssFinset`, degeneracy maps `O.degPts`, torsion subgroups `O.toricPts`, finite parts `O.finPts` (for $m$, the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion classes $y$ for which `O.pts y` satisfies `ExtendsToPlace Pl Λ.σA`), and special-fibre dictionary `O.ptsSp` identifying the glued Picard group `GluedPic0 (ResidueField Pl) (Fbar p M H hpM (ResidueField Pl)) O.ssFinset` with the sections of `O.g` over `resPt Pl` followed by `Λ.σA`.
--
--   *Representability and Abel–Jacobi pins.* `hD` and `hDQ` assert that the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the $\Gamma_M$-model over $R_p$, respectively of its base change to $\mathbf Q$, cut out by `algEquivZeroCut` with rigidification along `𝔛.εinf`, is represented by the designation built from `O.G`, `O.g` and the unit section; `hsep` requires the base-changed curve over $\mathbf Q$ to be separated. Further data: a section `ajQ` over $\mathbf Q$ into the base-changed designation, a comparison morphism `kQ` between the pullbacks of the model along `genPt p` and along `specMap (R p) ℚ`, a morphism `ajbar : 𝔛.Meta.C ⟶ O.G` and a point `εbar` of `𝔛.Meta.C` over the base. The accompanying hypotheses are: `hpoinc`, an isomorphism of the Poincaré bundle of `hDQ` with the base change to $\mathbf Q$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hD`; `hajQε`, that the cusp section followed by `ajQ` is the zero section; `hajQ`, that for every field $K$, every morphism $t : \mathrm{Spec}\,K \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathbf Q$ and every section $x$ of the base-changed curve over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along $x$ followed by `ajQ` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the cusp at $t$ (so that `ajQ` is the Abel–Jacobi morphism $x \mapsto [x - \infty]$); `hkQ₁` and `hkQ₂`, the compatibilities of `kQ` with the two projections (the second up to `specMap ℚ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`); `hajbar`, that `ajbar` is `𝔛.eeta` followed by `kQ`, `ajQ` and the first projection; `hajbar_over`, that `ajbar` followed by `O.g` is `𝔛.Meta.toBase` followed by `genPt p`; `hεbar`, that `εbar` is the cusp point; `hεbar_aj`, that `εbar` followed by `ajbar` is the zero point; `hpts_law`, that `O.pts` is additive for the relative group law obtained from `hD`; and `hAJ`, that for all points $x$ and $s$ of `𝔛.Meta.C` with $s$ the cusp there is a degree-zero divisor $D$ equal to $(\mathrm{place}\,x) - (\mathrm{place}\,s)$ with `(O.pts (Pic0.mk D)).1` equal to $x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   *The coefficient ring $R$.* A commutative domain $R$ is given which is a Henselian local ring with algebraically closed residue field, an algebra over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with faithful scalar action, whose image lies in `Pl` (`hRA`), which is a discrete valuation ring (`hRdvr`) in which $p$ is irreducible (`hRirr`), and which cuts out the inertia group in the two senses: an element of $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbf Q)$ lies in `Pl.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` exactly when it fixes the image of $R$ pointwise (`hRfix`), and every element of `Pl` fixed by that inertia group comes from $R$ (`hRmax`).
--
--   *$p$-divisible groups.* A [`PDivisibleGroup R p h`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199) $\mathcal G$ is given (levels `𝒢.level v`, finite free $R$-Hopf algebras of rank $p^{vh}$, with surjective transition maps whose kernels are the $p^{v}$-torsion ideals), together with an injective additive map $\Delta$ from `𝒢.Points (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` to `JH M H` such that: `hΔlev`, for every $v$ the subgroup `O.finPts (p ^ v)` is exactly the image under $\Delta$ of the level-$v$ points; `hΔgal`, $\Delta$ is equivariant for the Galois action through $R$-semilinear automorphisms; and `hΔhecke`, every generator $g$ of [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) is induced, through $\Delta$, by a family of coalgebra-algebra endomorphisms $\varphi_v$ of the levels compatible with the transition maps. A second $p$-divisible group $\mathcal B$ of height $h_B$ is given with maps $\psi_v : \mathcal B.\mathrm{level}\,v \to \mathcal G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, and integers with $h =$ `O.toricRank` $+\, h_B$ (`hhB`) and $h_B = 2h'$ (`hhB2`). The hypotheses on $\psi$ are: `hψt`, compatibility with the transition maps; `hψker`, that a level-$v$ point of $\mathcal G$ has trivial image under $\psi_v$ exactly when its $\Delta$-image lies in `O.toricPts (p ^ v)`; `hψsurj`, surjectivity of $\psi_v$ on points; `hψred`, that if the $\psi_v$-image of a point reduces to the identity (all values of `Pl.valuation` on the differences with the counit are $< 1$) then so does the point itself; and `hperiod`, that for every $v$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia group, every $p^{v}$-torsion class $z$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and every level-$v$ point $y$ with $\Delta y = \sigma \cdot z - z$, the $\psi_v$-image of $y$ reduces to the identity in the same valuative sense.
--
--   *Realisation of $\mathcal G$ inside `O.G`.* A ring homomorphism `ρh : R p →+* R` and morphisms `ι v : Spec (𝒢.level v) ⟶ O.G` are given with: `hρh`, compatibility of `ρh` with the algebra maps to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$; `hιbase`, that `ι v` lies over the base via `ρh`; `hιcl`, that the induced lift to the fibre product is a closed immersion; `hιp`, that `ι v` is killed by multiplication by $p^{v}$ in `O.L`; `hιpts`, that `ι v` realises `O.pts ∘ Δ` on level-$v$ points; `hιmul`, that `ι v` is multiplicative for points over any $R$-algebra $B$; `hιt`, compatibility with the transition maps; `hιhecke`, that each generator $g$ is induced on `ι` by endomorphisms $\varphi_v$ of the levels compatible with transitions, matching `O.hecke S g` and `genOpH M H S g`; and `hιfin` (three clauses, summarised here), that the lift $j_v$ of `ι v` into the fibre product of the $p^{v}$-kernel with $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$ is both an open and a closed immersion and that its image contains every point lying over the closed point of $R$.
--
--   *Semilinear and special-fibre pins.* `wgen` is a semilinear automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ (a pair of ring automorphisms compatible with the structure map) which, by `hwgen`, computes the effect of `𝔛.w` on places. A homomorphism `ρ : R p →+* Pl` is given compatible with the algebra map to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ (`hρ`), with `Λ.σA = Spec.map ρ` (`hσA`). The hypothesis `hsp` (a configured-point pin, its many binders summarised here) asserts: for $i \in$ `Fin 2`, for points $y_1, y_2$ of `𝔛.Meta.C`, sections $u_1, u_2$ of the $\Gamma_M$-model over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho$ matching $y_1, y_2$ and landing in `𝔛.smoothLocus`, residue-field points $u_{\kappa 1}, u_{\kappa 2}$ of the fibre compatible with them, closed points $P_1, P_2$ of `(𝔛.Mfib …).C` whose images under `𝔛.efib` followed by `𝔛.comp … i` are the closed points of $u_{\kappa 1}, u_{\kappa 2}$, a degree-zero divisor $D$ equal to $(\mathrm{place}\,y_1) - (\mathrm{place}\,y_2)$, and an admissible gluing datum $x$ whose first component is $(\mathrm{place}\,P_1) - (\mathrm{place}\,P_2)$ if $i = 0$ and $0$ otherwise, whose second component is that same divisor if $i = 1$ and $0$ otherwise, and whose third component is $0$, there exists a section $s$ of `O.g` over `Λ.σA` with `(O.pts (Pic0.mk D)).1 = barPt Pl ≫ s.1` and with `O.ptsSp.symm` of the restriction of $s$ along `resPt Pl` equal to the class of $x$ in `GluedPic0`. The hypothesis `hspΛ` is the analogous pin at the $\Lambda$-level (binders summarised here), with the closed points $Q_1, Q_2$ specified through `fibreMap` of `𝔛.π` or `𝔛.πw` according as $i = 0$ or not, and with conclusion: there exists a section $s_0$ of `Λ.f` over `Λ.σA` with `(Λ.pts (O.degPts i (Pic0.mk D))).1 = barPt Pl ≫ s₀.1` and `Λ.ptsSp.symm` of its restriction equal to the class of the prescribed degree-zero divisor $(\mathrm{place}\,Q_1) - (\mathrm{place}\,Q_2)$ on the special fibre. The hypothesis `hdia0` asserts that for every $e \in (\mathbf Z/(M/p))^{\times}$ and every closed point $P$ of `(𝔛.Mfib …).C`, transporting $P$ along the fibre map of `𝔛.dia0 e` again gives a closed point, whose place is the image of the place of $P$ under the semilinear automorphism attached to `diamondActionModL` applied to [`CuspForm.gammaLift (M / p) e`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L36).
--
--   *Frobenius, diamond and degeneracy operators on the special fibre.* Additive endomorphisms $F$, $F^{-1}$ and $F^{*}$ of the Picard group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `Fbar p M H hpM (ResidueField Pl)` are given with $F$ the Frobenius pushforward `qExpFrobeniusPushforwardModL` at level $\Gamma_N$ (`hF`), with $F$ and $F^{-1}$ mutually inverse (`hFinv`), and $F^{*}z = p\,F^{-1}z$ (`hFstar`). A unit `pb` of $\mathbf Z/(M/p)$ whose underlying value is $p$ (`hpb`) determines the diamond operator $\delta$, the action of `diamondActionModL` applied to [`CuspForm.gammaLift (M / p) pb`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L36) (`hδ`). Degeneracy data: additive maps `αpull i : JH (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) →+ JH M H` and sections `degPull i` of `O.g` over `Λ.f` for $i \in$ `Fin 2`, with `hpull` stating that `O.pts (αpull i x)` is `Λ.pts x` followed by `degPull i`, and `hpullsp` stating that for every section $x$ of `Λ.f` over `resPt Pl` followed by `Λ.σA`, the pair `GluedPic0.toPic0Pair O.ssFinset` of `O.ptsSp.symm` of $x$ followed by `degPull i` equals $(\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}x,\ F^{*}\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}x)$ when $i = 0$ and $(F^{*}\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}x,\ \delta\,\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}x)$ otherwise. An additive endomorphism `Wbar` of `JH M H` is given by the action of `wgen` (`hWbar`), and `hUPgen` states the generic identity $U_p x + \overline W x = \alpha^{*}_1(\deg_0 x)$, i.e. `genOpH M H S (CohCarrier.Gen.U p _ hpM) x + Wbar x = αpull 1 (O.degPts 0 x)` for all $x$. Finally `hpull_mul` states that each `degPull i` carries the group law `Λ.L` to `O.L` on sections over an arbitrary base.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every element $x$ of the $p$-torsion subgroup `Pic0.torsion (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (xHFunctionFieldBar M H) p` of `JH M H`, if the underlying class lies in the image under [`TateModule.proj p (JH M H) 1`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L122) (evaluation at index $1$) of the additive subgroup underlying the corner submodule [`IharaLemma.cornerSubmodule (S'.e i₀)`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L46), that is of $e_{i_0}\,T_p(J_H)$, and if it lies in `O.finPts p`, then for every section $s$ of `O.g` over `Λ.σA` such that `(O.pts x).1 = barPt Pl ≫ s.1` and such that the second component of `GluedPic0.toPic0Pair O.ssFinset` applied to `O.ptsSp.symm` of the restriction of $s$ along `resPt Pl` is zero, the class `O.ptsSp.symm` of that restriction is itself zero.
--
--   This is the injectivity step for the reduction map on the ordinary corner at $p$: on the finite part of the $p$-torsion cut out by the ordinary idempotent $e_{i_0}$, the reduction of a section to the special fibre is determined by one of its two glued coordinates, so that vanishing of the $\Sigma^0$-coordinate forces the whole glued class to vanish. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the Atkin–Lehner translate, in [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.toPic0Pair_ptsSp_symm_atkinLehner_fst_eq_zero_iff_exists_point_reducesToOne_of_mem_corner_of_mem_finPts_bridgePins`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.toPic0Pair_ptsSp_symm_atkinLehner_fst_eq_zero_iff_exists_point_reducesToOne_of_mem_corner_of_mem_finPts_bridgePins), and rests on the block form of $U_p$ on the glued special-fibre coordinates together with the characterisation of the finite part by extension of sections to the place.
